{
  "opening": "This release introduces significant improvements to the command-line interface, specifically enhancing the robustness and extensibility of the pysemver subcommands. It also adds new validation capabilities to help users identify and handle invalid version strings effectively.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m19",
      "text": "The cmd_check function must accept parsed arguments containing a version string and return None if the version is valid, or raise a ValueError if it is not. The cmd_bump function must accept parsed arguments specifying a bump type and return the resulting bumped version as a string. The cmd_compare function must accept parsed arguments with two versions and return '-1', '0', or '1' as a string to indicate their relative order."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure these observable behaviors are strictly maintained in the public API to guarantee consistent tooling interactions."
}
